00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.189 align:start position:0%
 
center of the u.s southern border  opening up to fully vaccinated travelers  yesterday putting additional strains on  security along the u.s mexico border  brandon judd is president of the  national border patrol council he joins  us now clearly this is a good thing  for commerce on texas border towns and  cities but there are questions that with  customs and border patrol under such  pressure already  uh because of so many different issues  as to whether or not you can adequately  vet the people who are coming across the  border now that it's reopened what are  your concerns  yeah the the chamber of commerce the  local businesses they've been asking  that the ports of entry be open for a  long time now and and i understand why  they their businesses have taken a  nosedive ever since the covet 19  pandemic and ever since we shut down the  the ports of entry to non-essential  travel but if you look at it from a law  enforcement standpoint and that's what i  have to look at it from  when you look at it from that aspect  this is not the right time to do this  simply because we are in the biggest  crisis border security crisis that we've  ever faced in the history of this  country and when you don't put policies  in place when you don't put programs or  operations in place that help us to  control the traffic that's coming into  the united states and pulling these  officers out of the field and putting  them back at the ports of entry  that's just going to open up gaps that's  going to allow cartels to exploit more  of our vulnerabilities and it's going to  allow more drugs to come into the united  states which we know are killing  children by the thousands  and so again from a law enforcement  standpoint this is not the right time to  do this so what's the answer to this man  because obviously you've got competing  interests here you've got the law  enforcement component of it but you also  have the commerce component of it you  have families who haven't seen each  other for 20 months who were so happy to  be reunited as people came across the  border yesterday is is there a way to  sort of balance both things or does it  have to be one or the other  no it doesn't have to be one or the  other we can actually secure the border  with the number of border patrol agents  that we have we can send the cpp  officers back to the ports of entry but  you have to have the proper policy if  you don't have policy in place that is  going to hold people in custody pending  their deportation or asylum hearings  we're going to open that floodgate it's  going to be that magnet that draws so  many people here so this administration  again what they what they refuse to  recognize what they've refused to assess  and address is the policy that they can  put in place that is going to help us  secure the border i don't need more  infrastructure more manpower more  technology i need policy president trump  proved that and of course as these  ground ports of entry have reopened  elsewhere along the border criminal  activity continues compiled just some  headlines from customs and border  protection media releases in the last  week take a look at this calexico agents  arrest sereno gang member over the  weekend multiple criminal migrants  arrested in the rio grande valley border  patrol agents kept a large group near  eagle pass multiple criminal migrants  arrested at the border hidalgo migrant  smuggler  endangers children at the arizona border  so so now we've we've as you point out  taken a lot of these agents out of the  field put them at the ports of entry and  meantime there's nothing that suggests  that cross-border criminal activity  outside of the ports of entry is slowing  what  down  just explained there if that doesn't  define crisis i don't know what does  everything that you said is what we're  dealing with on a daily basis and on top  of that you just talk with william  loginess about  people that are entering the country and  claiming to be 17 years old i can  personally tell you that when we take  somebody in custody the burden of proof  is on us to show that they are not who  they say that they are and if we can't  prove that then we have to treat them as  if they they are 17 when in reality  they're 24. i can tell you we see people  all the time who look if they look a day  younger than 21 i'd be surprised but we  have to treat them as if they are 17 if  they claim that if we cannot get the  cooperation from other countries or if  we don't have the time to do that so all  of these things when you stack all of  these things together you clearly see  that we just don't have control of the  border and this administration isn't  doing anything or putting programs in  place that is going to help us get  control of the border all right brandon  judd head of the national border patrol  council always good to be with you thank  you sir appreciate it  thank you john hi everyone i'm brian  kilmeade i want you to do me a favor i  want you to click to subscribe to the  fox news youtube page this is the only  way that i know for sure that you're not  going to miss any great commentary any  great news bites any great interviews  coming your way on fox you can get it  all here on youtube so subscribe right  now

